.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt RETICULUM-GO-SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm reticulum-go-sh , rgosh
.Nd interactive remote shell over Reticulum
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm reticulum-go Cm sh
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl compat
.Op Fl line
.Op Fl raw
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Ar destination_hash command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Provides an SSH-like interactive shell over an encrypted Reticulum link and
channel. The native protocol uses destination app
.Dq rgosh .
Connecting to a Python rnsh destination hash selects the rnsh wire protocol automatically.
.Fl compat
forces that protocol.
.Pp
Listen mode
.Pq Fl l
accepts sessions. Without
.Fl compat
it listens on both the rgosh and rnsh destination hashes. Initiator mode takes a
destination hash and an optional remote command.
.Sh FLAG PARSING
Before the first positional argument, all flags belong to rgosh. After the first
positional argument, only multi-letter rgosh flags are still parsed. Single-letter
arguments there belong to the remote command. Once remote command text begins,
every remaining argument belongs to the remote command. A literal
.Cm --
ends flag parsing.
.Pp
For example,
.Cm rgosh -l /bin/sh -config /etc/rns
treats
.Fl config
as an rgosh flag, while
.Cm rgosh <hash> ls -l
passes
.Fl l
to the remote command.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--no-announce"
.It Fl config Ar path
Config file or directory. A directory uses the file named config inside it.
.It Fl i Ar path
Identity file.
.It Fl p
Print the full identity hash and full listening destination hashes, then exit.
With
.Fl json ,
print one JSON object with plain hex values and no angle brackets.
.It Fl m
Mirror the remote exit code as the local exit code. Without it, a nonzero remote
exit does not set the local exit code.
.It Fl b Ar seconds
Listen announce interval. The default is 900 seconds. Zero announces only at startup.
Startup announces are repeated about 3, 10, and 30 seconds after the first announce
so interfaces that finish connecting late still receive one. Positive values continue
periodic announces at that interval.
.It Fl no-announce
Never announce in listen mode.
.It Fl a Ar hash
Allowed remote identity hash. Repeatable. Bare 32-character hex and angle-bracketed
hex are accepted. Truncated hashes are rejected.
.It Fl n
Accept sessions from anyone.
.It Fl N
Do not identify to the listener.
.It Fl C
Reject a remote command line and run only the listener default command.
.It Fl A
Append the remote command line to the listener default command.
.It Fl w Ar seconds
Path and link timeout. Zero uses an adaptive timeout from interface bitrate.
.El
.Sh ALLOWED IDENTITIES
Listen mode reads these files:
.Pa /etc/rgosh/allowed_identities ,
.Pa ~/.config/rgosh/allowed_identities ,
.Pa ~/.rgosh/allowed_identities ,
.Pa /etc/rnsh/allowed_identities ,
.Pa ~/.config/rnsh/allowed_identities ,
and
.Pa ~/.rnsh/allowed_identities .
Files are read again for each new link.
.Pp
Each line contains one full 32-character hexadecimal identity hash. Angle brackets
are accepted. Blank lines and lines whose first non-space character is
.Cm #
are ignored. Invalid lines are skipped. Command-line
.Fl a
values are checked strictly and invalid values fail startup.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Client mode returns zero after a clean remote command unless an error occurs.
Use
.Fl m
when the local exit status must equal the remote command status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reticulum-go 1 ,
.Xr reticulum-go-x 1
